Review all three comparison categories:

EXISTING:
Verify whether each matched registry type adequately covers the candidate. Reconsider candidates that express genuinely distinct semantic relationships.

NEW:
Verify that each candidate has sufficient trajectory support, appropriate granularity, and semantic meaning not adequately covered by the existing registry.

UNCERTAIN:
Resolve whether each candidate is adequately covered by an existing type or represents a distinct new relationship.

Select the valid relationship types that add genuinely new semantic meaning to the existing registry.

